1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,400
[On-screen text] Welcome to HAT-Lab. The page introduces the study platform and asks the participant to click Continue.

2
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:12,000
[Visual] The interface opens the scenario list. Available agents appear as cards, including Cover Letter Agent and HR Agent.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:34,000
[Visual] The participant expands the HR Agent card. The task description asks them to choose the best candidate for a Java Engineer role.

4
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:53,000
[Visual] The participant continues browsing the scenario cards before starting a task with the agent.

5
00:00:53,000 --> 00:01:06,000
[Visual] The chat workspace opens. The agent asks the participant to upload a job description for a cover-letter task.

6
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:14,000
[Visual] The participant interacts with the agent chat. The left panel shows the current task materials and instructions.

7
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:54,000
[Visual] After the agent produces an output, a post-scenario survey appears. The first question asks whether anything unusual was noticed.

8
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:00,000
[Visual] The participant answers the anomaly-perception item and continues through the remaining scenario questions.

9
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:20,000
[Visual] Additional post-scenario items appear, including ratings and short free-text responses about the agent's output.

10
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:36,000
[Visual] The post-experiment survey begins. One item asks how the participant's trust in AI agents changed after learning about the study.

11
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:55,000
[Visual] Later survey pages ask about future caution with AI agents and preferred defense strategies for agent-related threats.

12
00:02:55,000 --> 00:03:19,381
[On-screen text] Thank you for your participation. The page confirms that the study session is complete and that the response has been recorded.
